{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to HaShem: Please, Adonai.</b> You are stationing me against men who know seventy languages, who stand before Pharaoh — and if one of them speaks to me in his language and I do not know how to reply, will they not laugh at me? And I would say: an emissary of whom are you, that you do not know how to hear and understand every language? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״Who set a mouth for the first man״ — to call names for all creatures, as it is said: ״ויקרא שמות שם״ — 'שם' is not written but rather 'שמות' (names), teaching that he called them names in seventy languages. And I also gave him [a mouth], when I said to him: ״המן העץ וגו'״, and he said to me: ״האשה אשר נתת עמדי״. How much more so for you, who come to redeem My children. Another interpretation: ״Who set a mouth״ — meaning, a new mouth I create; how much more so do I repair yours, which needs only a slight repair. From Rabbi Yosef. And Rabbi Ovadiah explained: What do you mean to mention that you are heavy of mouth? ״Who set a mouth for man״ — ״אנכי ה'״, and I Myself made even your mouth; therefore I know that you are heavy of mouth, and it is in My hand to repair it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:42.972949585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}